{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1528620-is-there-a-way-to-bring-the-lost-pantheon-back-following-2e-rules","id":1528620,"title":"Is there a way to bring the Lost Pantheon back following 2e rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-15T13:57:44-08:00","id":1528620,"title":"Is there a way to bring the Lost Pantheon back following 2e rules?","content":"Hi guys. So, I love the Lost Pantheon from the 1e book Lords of Summer. Changelings posing as Gods, perhaps being the gods depending on your point of view? Hell yeah!<br /> but I don't know to bring them to 2e, Rules as written. Can anybody help? Are they still a Entitlement? Or maybe a Lost Dynasty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T14:58:14-08:00","id":1528623,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they could work as a special form of Dramaturgy- perhaps a &quot;modified splat&quot; of some sort (not unlike, let's say, Goblin Queens and Empty Hearts), which allows the Changeling to take the &quot;role&quot; of a god as part of a contract between them and a mortal community, with some hints about &quot;this might be how the first Gentry came into existence, humanity's own gods who follow ancient contracts long forgotten by those who signed them yet are still valid&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T15:22:39-08:00","id":1528624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1528620-is-there-a-way-to-bring-the-lost-pantheon-back-following-2e-rules?p=1528623#post1528623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they could work as a special form of Dramaturgy- perhaps a &quot;modified splat&quot; of some sort (not unlike, let's say, Goblin Queens and Empty Hearts), which allows the Changeling to take the &quot;role&quot; of a god as part of a contract between them and a mortal community, with some hints about &quot;this might be how the first Gentry came into existence, humanity's own gods who follow ancient contracts long forgotten by those who signed them yet are still valid&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>is there an 2e update to dramaturhy? i don't remember rn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T17:36:04-08:00","id":1528628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1528620-is-there-a-way-to-bring-the-lost-pantheon-back-following-2e-rules?p=1528624#post1528624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there an 2e update to dramaturhy? i don't remember rn</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramaturgy is a 2e thing detailed in Kith &amp; Kin. There's not much to it mechanically besides the introduction of a form of fae identity theft and a couple of Merits interacting with Loopholes, with the narrative addition of &quot;this is basically what hobgoblin deals are made to power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lost Pantheon as a unified Noble Order is gone, but nothing prevents there from being a recurring variety of blazon for changelings who've styled themselves as gods. We haven't got any hard rules for eldritch entitlements, but Oak Ash &amp; Thorn's existing mechanics are as solid a starting point as any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T18:12:17-08:00","id":1528631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1528620-is-there-a-way-to-bring-the-lost-pantheon-back-following-2e-rules?p=1528628#post1528628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dramaturgy is a 2e thing detailed in Kith &amp; Kin. There's not much to it mechanically besides the introduction of a form of fae identity theft and a couple of Merits interacting with Loopholes, with the narrative addition of &quot;this is basically what hobgoblin deals are made to power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lost Pantheon as a unified Noble Order is gone, but nothing prevents there from being a recurring variety of blazon for changelings who've styled themselves as gods. We haven't got any hard rules for eldritch entitlements, but Oak Ash &amp; Thorn's existing mechanics are as solid a starting point as any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Satchel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T01:46:41-08:00","id":1528639,"title":"","content":"<b>The Lost Pantheon</b><br /> <br /> <i>Where have all the old gods gone? Right here.</i><br /> <br /> All myths sprang from the gods. Once, they were worshipped throughout the world, but as science and technology winnowed away belief in their power, they slipped into dreams and dusty tomes. Babylonian, Egyptian, Greek, Norse\u2026 their empires have fallen. Their domains have been left untended for too long. They are all Lost.<br /> <br /> But not the Lost Pantheon. By taking on godly guises, its members raise divine hands to ensure souls are ferried, new ground is consecrated, and inspiration is meted out to the worthy. Along the way, they restore faith in a world left wanting. The wait has been long, but now, the Ancients wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges and Duties</b><br /> <br /> Unlike most legion entitlements, the Lost Pantheon theoretically has no limit on its membership: As long as humans have gods, the Pantheon can stand for them. However, only one Ancient represent a given deity at a time. One Baldur, one Juno, one Horus. Still, few know how many are embodied within this entitlement at present, and it\u2019s rare for a freehold to have more than one member in its bounds. When they do cross paths, they\u2019re more likely to come to blows over mythological grudges than they are to work together.<br /> <br /> The specific duties of each Pantheon member vary with the godly roles they take on, but every domain includes the following: the maintenance of at least one [REDACTED], preserving or stoking its presence within the Hedge and keeping the paths open so its power can flow into the mortal world; maintaining at least one temple, such as restoring a ruin from antiquity, consecrating a Hollow, or running gatherings for initiates; and protecting the interests and safety of a dedicated type of follower (children, mothers, farmers, scholars, etc.).<br /> <br /> Wherever an Ancient wanders, they must uphold their deity\u2019s ideals. To embody Artemis, one must forswear the touch of men and join in the hunt; to embody Idunn, he must tend and defend an orchard of Goblin Fruit. Thus elevated, they attract prayer, and pilgrims seek them to resolve issues within their purview: They protect against pollution, incursion, gentrification, or just Fae interference. A member of the Lost Pantheon might rescue an injured animal sacred to her, take in a child orphaned by an eruption of her element, or protect a changeling of the profession she blesses.<br /> <br /> To better carry out her divine duties, her capacity for the fantastic deepens. Events that might shake another\u2019s Clarity merely force them to reconsider. The Gates of Ivory stand forever open, their consciousnesses alert whether their flesh wakes or sleeps.<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry Token: Celestial Medallions (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> In its Mask, a Celestial Medallion resembles an old, battered coin or some other metallic token from antiquity, usually from a country where the Ancient\u2019s god originated. Behind the Mask, it\u2019s a glorious electrum star with nine points, its central motif representing a specific deity incorporated into the stone chair on the entitlement\u2019s heraldry (Athena\u2019s Aegis, Thor\u2019s Mjolnir, etc.). No two are exactly alike.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>Unlike most heraldry tokens, a Celestial Medallion can\u2019t be stolen, at least not for long. The bond between this token and its manifested deity is strong, and the Wyrd ensures it returns to its rightful keeper\u2019s hand within 24 hours of its removal.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-16-2024, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T02:48:15-08:00","id":1528641,"title":"","content":"Thanks Yossarian!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}